## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The junction was under sustained, near-unbroken congestion for the entire 60-minute period, with no quiet phase. Mins 0–24 showed heavy but flowing mixed traffic with many identifiable plates; mins 25–55 were the worst, with all lanes packed and near-stationary (gridlock peaking mins 50–55), during which pedestrian movement between queued vehicles became routine and plate readability dropped. Mins 56–59 saw traffic resume movement while remaining heavy. Dominant traffic was private cars (overwhelmingly white) with very high two-wheeler and auto-rickshaw participation. Recurring elements: the pink/red hatchback, the blue three-wheeler goods carrier, red tractors with tankers, red open-top off-road vehicles, Nirma University and red city buses, and pedestrians (including children and elderly persons) walking in live traffic throughout — a persistent safety concern at this location.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. Traffic was heavy across the full 60 minutes; the closest to relief was mins 56–59, when flow resumed but remained heavy.
