## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The scene is a permanently busy signalised city junction whose character changes mainly with the light. Evening (minutes 0–199) shows steady moderate traffic with a near-ritualistic white hatchback crossing left-to-right around the 30s mark of almost every minute, alongside buses, autos and regular rain-wet roads. After midnight (minutes 200–299) the mix shifts decisively toward two-wheelers and green-and-yellow auto-rickshaws with large pedestrian crowds idling by the right-side shops. The quietest stretch is the pre-dawn (roughly minutes 300–524): very light, free-flowing traffic, almost no pedestrians, heavy vehicles (mixers, tippers, goods lorries, intercity coaches) forming a large share of what moves. From dawn (approx. 525 onward) traffic and pedestrian activity rebuild gradually, with city buses (DTC-style red/blue-and-white), delivery three-wheelers and commuter two-wheelers increasingly dominant, and by minutes 650–719 queues begin forming at red signals. The "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" red-light-enforcement overlay recurs across the whole period, as do amber/red signal phases facing the camera, wet/reflective roads after periodic rain, dogs on the carriageway, and occasional emergency/official vehicles with beacons. Only one incident of any substance appears — the apparent collision at minute 599 — and the system raised no alerts in 720 minutes.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
